┌─ Thora's story ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                                                                                             │
│  You were born to farming folk, who had little but gave what they had. You were named for a grandparent     │
│  you never met, and told every year how little you resembled them.                                          │
│                                                                                                             │
│  A winter wolf came into the yard when you were six, and you faced it with a stick until the grown folk     │
│  came. The story grew; so did you. At fourteen you stood in the levy with a borrowed spear, and found you   │
│  had a taste for it.                                                                                        │
│                                                                                                             │
│  You were promised once, and the promise was broken, and you have not made another. Fortune never found     │
│  your door; whatever you have, you got yourself.                                                            │
│                                                                                                             │
│  You left, as the young do, because staying was the one thing you could not bear. You came to the Hall by   │
│  the road everyone comes by.                                                                                │
│                                                                                                             │
│ Esc close                                                                                                   │
